Myth: Long ago, Sound had a twin sister named Silence, and the two were inseparable yet opposite in nature. Sound danced and sang across the world, filling every space with music and voice. Silence followed behind, creating peaceful pauses between Sound's exuberant melodies.

One day, they quarreled. Sound declared, "I bring life and joy to the world! Without me, there would be nothing!" Silence replied softly, "But without me, your songs would have no meaning. There would be no rest, no anticipation, no space for listening."

Angry, they separated. Sound filled the entire world with constant noise—birds never stopped singing, winds never ceased howling, voices never paused. At first, people celebrated, but soon they grew exhausted and overwhelmed. They could no longer distinguish one sound from another, and everything became meaningless chaos.

Realizing her mistake, Sound sought out her sister. "You were right," she admitted. "I need you to give my voice purpose."

Silence embraced her twin, and together they created rhythm—the heartbeat of the universe. From that day forward, they worked as one, teaching the world that beauty lives not in sound alone, nor silence alone, but in the sacred dance between them.
